   2429  f752							; NO REFP1 write here (2026-10-22): REFP1 is ONE register for GRP1, but a
   2430  f752							; frame can draw TWO objects (band pairing, or the 1-of-2 rotation). Driving
   2431  f752							; it from the ACTIVE object made the mirrored miner flip sides every other
   2432  f752							; frame in any room that also had another object. The miner's mirror is
   2433  f752							; gone (a design-based mirror like the LAMP's type 13 needs 32 more art
   2434  f752							; bytes and the table ends 6 B below the $F8C0 pin), so every GRP1 object
   2435  f752							; is drawn unmirrored and REFP1 stays 0 — the bank1 HUD writes 0 for its
   2436  f752							; score, which is exactly what the cave wants.
   2437  f752							; Set ObjTop for kernel GRP1 visibility check.
   2438  f752							; S2.2: ObjTop stored RoomY-relative (ObjTopRel = ActiveObjectY-RoomY+1) so
   2439  f752							; the kernel compares against running-Y (`tya`) instead of `lda Scanline`
   2440  f752							; — frees 9c/line (lda Scanline + inc Scanline) for the laser beam write.
   2441  f752							; Kernel .Grp1 does: tya / sec / sbc ObjTop / cmp #OBJ_WINDOW / bcs.
