   4090  fe0d							; ==============================================================================
   4091  fe0d							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   4092  fe0d							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   4093  fe0d							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   4094  fe0d							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   4095  fe0d							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   4096  fe0d							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   4097  fe0d							;
   4098  fe0d							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   4099  fe0d							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   4100  fe0d							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   4101  fe0d							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   4102  fe0d							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   4103  fe0d							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   4104  fe0d							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   4105  fe0d							;
   4106  fe0d							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   4107  fe0d							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   4108  fe0d							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   4109  fe0d							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   4110  fe0d							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
   4111  fe0d							; ==============================================================================
